  "ingredients": [
    "2 cups all-purpose flour",
    "2 cups semolina flour",
    "1 pinch salt",
    "6 large eggs",
    "2 tablespoons olive oil"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/FPw0uWnIYrwfUSJryD3-mKIKqa4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/17662-fresh-semolina-and-egg-pasta-Step-01-af5436bed2364f628012e7b35c498ad9.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/17662/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sift all-purpose flour, semolina flour, and a pinch of salt together in a large bowl. Make a mountain out of flour mixture on a clean surface; create a deep well in the center. Break eggs into the well and add olive oil. Whisk eggs very gently with a fork, gradually incorporating flour from the sides of the well. When mixture becomes too thick to mix with a fork, begin kneading with your hands.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/NLjOXyIpeqISFgkP9g0Y4AHh-Zc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/17662-fresh-semolina-and-egg-pasta-Step-03-f5da800110444cb5bc9f5a9be80607f6.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/17662/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Knead dough until it is smooth and supple, 8 to 12 minutes, Dust dough and work surface with semolina as needed to keep dough from becoming sticky. Wrap dough tightly in plastic wrap; allow it to rest at room temperature for 30 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/8ZrpLNiK8MxJOlvY2ZWG8f-FioU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/17662-fresh-semolina-and-egg-pasta-Step-04-8d3a39ed96c1448a84c2cfc195ea30ac.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/17662/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roll out dough with a pasta machine or a rolling pin to desired thickness. Cut into your favorite style of noodle or stuff with your favorite filling to make ravioli.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/eK9udKVstghD2qLJVZ1_DNxz86s=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/17662-fresh-semolina-and-egg-pasta-Step-05-3d917794f786458eabf03f8eb776ea43.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/17662/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bring a large pot of lightly salted water to a boil. Cook pasta in the boiling water until tender yet firm to the bite, 1 to 3 minutes (or longer depending on thickness). Drain immediately and toss with your favorite sauce.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/v--j12OEaM0pbsHABDkP5yvUvbM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/17662-fresh-semolina-and-egg-pasta-Beauty-3x4-1-b5b323cc013540d6be591b3cfdbc3daa.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/17662/step_05.webp"
    }
  ],
